ÔªøProcessing tile size (mm)
Size of a tile during processing. Decrease to 
reduce GPU memory consumption, in particular if 
slicing generates an out of GPU memory error. 
Typical values are between 5 mm and 100 mm.ÔªøDiscretization step in xy (mm)
Smaller values increase precision on paths, but 
require more GPU memory and longer processing times.
Typical values are between 0.01mm and 0.1mm. 
Decrease processing tile size if the slicer reports 
an out of GPU memory error.ÔªøSlice to ribbons
Produces a mesh from the slices [.stl]
The mesh is generated by only producing vertical
sides from the slice contours. While completely
open, the mesh can be processed successfully by 
most external slicers. ÔªøSlice thickness (mm)
