Produces instructions for a laser cutter [.gcode]ÔªøCutting speed (mm/sec)
Laser cutting speed (millimeters per second). Reduce
to cut deeper at the same power level.ÔªøFocused beam width (mm)
Diameter (millimeters) of the focused laser impact.ÔªøBed size y (mm)
Size (in millimeters) of printing bed, front to back.ÔªøPower multiplier
Power multiplier when cutting with this brush.ÔªøTravel speed (mm/sec)
Laser travel speed (when not cutting) in millimeters per second (mm/sec)ÔªøSpeed multiplier
Printing speed multiplier for this brush. This can
be used to change the printing speed locally,
using different brushes in different parts of the
object. ÔªøDiscretization step in xy (mm)
Smaller values increase precision, but require 
more GPU memory and longer processing times.
Typical values are between 0.01mm/pixels and 
0.1mm/pixels. Decrease processing tile size if 
the slicer reports on out of GPU memory error.ÔªøCutting outline height (mm)
Cutting height in millimeters (mm) relative to object's bottom side
