ÔªøDistribution of slopes
Values closer to zero mean 'most infill walls have their slopes
close to the overhang angle' while values closer to 1 mean 'most
walls are vertical'.Direction of anisotropy
Orientation in the xy plane, in degrees, of the streched
cells produced by the degree of anisotropy.Degree of anisotropy
As this value decreases, the cells become more stretched
in the direction of anisotropy.Base cell size
A cell in a sponge-like structure can be thought as
an 'empty bubble'. This value changes the size of
'bubbles' and directly affects the infill density.ÔªøPaint to specify seam locationsÔªøPrint speed on first layer (mm/sec)
Printing speed (millimeters per second) for the 
first layer. Usually this is set to a low speed to
increase adhesion.ÔªøPrint speed for supports (mm/sec)
Printing speed (millimeters per second) for supports.
Supports must be structurally sound but need not be
aesthetically pleasing since they are disposed of
after printing.ÔªøEnable cooling fan on first layer
Enable the filament cooling fan only for
the first layer.ÔªøExtruder used for printing supports
Specify the id of the extruder to be used for 
printing supports (if generated).ÔªøTower size along X (mm)
Size of the tower along X direction. Increase if the 
extruder is not properly primed (holes when the 
extruder resumes printing after a swap), or if the 
tower is not stable enough when it becomes tall.Ôªø## Application
